WEBVTT

00:01.430 --> 00:04.530
Leaving behind countless thousands of tears

00:04.530 --> 00:08.170
My thoughts travel the wilderness

00:08.170 --> 00:16.100
The wounds will heal someday,
so come, trust myself

00:21.250 --> 00:27.760
Under the scorching rays of the sun,
what thoughts cross your mind?

00:27.760 --> 00:33.700
What does your grief-stricken gaze reflect now?

00:33.700 --> 00:42.640
If I can keep from losing my way,
step by step, it should be easy

00:42.640 --> 00:47.410
Like the wind

00:47.410 --> 00:50.480
Leaving behind countless thousands of tears

00:50.480 --> 00:54.080
I travel the dawn-lit wilderness

00:54.080 --> 01:00.520
The wounds will heal someday,
so come, trust myself

01:00.520 --> 01:07.330
Don't be afraid, change is
nothing to be frightened of

01:07.330 --> 01:13.440
As long as you are yourself, I will be with you

01:13.440 --> 01:20.180
Dreaming of tranquil days

01:20.180 --> 01:27.410
The roadless journey continues

01:39.160 --> 01:42.460
What did you want to talk about?

01:42.460 --> 01:43.770
Nadie?

01:43.770 --> 01:47.200
It really wouldn't be
right not to tell you, right?

01:47.200 --> 01:50.640
Because it's something
that's very important to you...

01:52.710 --> 01:54.440
The truth is...

01:58.610 --> 02:04.490
I'm... an artificially made witch...

02:04.490 --> 02:07.320
But you don't have to worry.

02:07.320 --> 02:11.220
No matter what you are, I...

02:18.800 --> 02:20.500
Ellis?

02:21.900 --> 02:25.670
Good-bye, Nadie.

02:26.910 --> 02:29.880
W-Wait! Don't go!

02:29.880 --> 02:32.240
Ellis!

02:51.530 --> 02:53.590
A dream...

02:59.440 --> 03:02.710
I really should tell her...

03:02.710 --> 03:07.780
...everything that I know...

03:07.780 --> 03:12.250
Ellis does not know the
secret concerning her birth.

03:12.250 --> 03:14.950
That is what Nadie believed.

03:29.400 --> 03:30.810
What's wrong?

03:30.810 --> 03:32.710
Wh-What do you mean?

03:32.710 --> 03:36.280
You've been looking at me.

03:36.280 --> 03:38.410
I-It's not like I'm looking at you.

03:38.410 --> 03:40.320
Why would I be looking at you?

03:40.320 --> 03:41.810
Ahead.

03:46.790 --> 03:48.960
That sure scared me!

03:48.960 --> 03:51.890
Keep your eyes forward when
you're driving, you taco-head!

03:51.890 --> 03:53.900
You're the taco-head, Nadie.

03:53.900 --> 03:57.670
- Why?
- You were over the center line.

03:57.670 --> 03:59.930
Huh? I was?

03:59.930 --> 04:01.700
Yes.

04:01.700 --> 04:03.400
Sorry.

04:31.630 --> 04:33.790
It seems we've passed them.

04:36.000 --> 04:38.740
And now, for the news.

04:38.740 --> 04:40.480
In their investigation

04:40.480 --> 04:44.680
of massive bribery by
members of the defense industry,

04:44.680 --> 04:48.750
the FBI has arrested Senator Hans Ritgen.

04:48.750 --> 04:52.820
The Senator is also rumored to have
ties within the CIA and it is believed

04:52.820 --> 04:57.930
that the FBI will seek out a detailed
account of this matter as well.

04:57.930 --> 04:59.960
As things stand,

04:59.960 --> 05:02.460
the FBI could conceivably
end up investigating the CIA,

05:02.460 --> 05:05.470
- which would be an unprecedented situation.
- I will be right there.

05:05.470 --> 05:07.700
Those involved are...

05:07.700 --> 05:10.070
Project Leviathan...

05:10.070 --> 05:14.710
Resurrect witches, who supposedly
once existed in this world,

05:14.710 --> 05:17.550
monopolize their powers as a nation,

05:17.550 --> 05:20.780
and greatly enhance our national interests...

05:20.780 --> 05:24.650
Thinking about it now, it was a ridiculous plan.

05:24.650 --> 05:28.680
The project was canceled due to an accident.

05:29.920 --> 05:33.530
The project team, R-339, was cut down

05:33.530 --> 05:35.500
and its name has remained
as a post in the Agency

05:35.500 --> 05:39.670
as a department that
handles unsettled business.

05:39.670 --> 05:43.640
Yes, that's your room, Rosenberg.

05:43.640 --> 05:47.880
I hear you've been in
personal contact with Ritgen.

05:47.880 --> 05:50.810
- Yes.
- Why?

05:50.810 --> 05:53.010
You were having him act as your sponsor,

05:53.010 --> 05:57.390
and you were moving forward
with Project Leviathan once again...

05:57.390 --> 05:58.940
Isn't that right?

06:00.720 --> 06:03.420
Resurrecting witches was ultimately

06:03.420 --> 06:06.590
nothing more than the
foolish imaginings of scientists.

06:06.590 --> 06:10.570
So, why would you do this?

06:10.570 --> 06:14.070
The investigating authorities have
already begun their work quietly.

06:14.070 --> 06:18.840
This is a situation that we must
view with extreme apprehension.

06:18.840 --> 06:23.510
What that project cost the
nation, financially speaking...

06:23.510 --> 06:27.820
The numerous inhumane experiments
that were conducted in secrecy...

06:27.820 --> 06:31.590
If it becomes known that the Agency
was involved in such things back then,

06:31.590 --> 06:33.650
it will be a huge problem.

06:33.650 --> 06:37.930
We must take measures
before it gets to that point.

06:37.930 --> 06:41.160
Go on vacation for a while.

06:41.160 --> 06:43.930
You accepted bribes from Ritgen

06:43.930 --> 06:48.600
and leaked information to him that
would benefit his political activity.

06:48.600 --> 06:53.610
Needless to say, the Agency had
absolutely nothing to do with it.

06:53.610 --> 06:58.110
So you intend to make me the sole
scapegoat and protect the Agency?

06:58.110 --> 07:01.180
Not just the Agency. You as well.

07:01.180 --> 07:04.920
I will appeal to the authorities
to decide not to prosecute you.

07:04.920 --> 07:08.490
Of course, that's only if you admit your guilt.

07:08.490 --> 07:12.450
How about it? I don't believe
you have much of a choice here.

07:17.700 --> 07:21.670
Rosenberg is taking a leave of absence.

07:21.670 --> 07:23.570
Really?

07:23.570 --> 07:25.740
It seems another group that's separate from us

07:25.740 --> 07:27.840
has been taking action.

07:27.840 --> 07:30.980
If he has withdrawn from the frontline,

07:30.980 --> 07:36.920
for all intents and purposes,
Project Leviathan is as good as suspended.

07:36.920 --> 07:38.820
Yes...

07:46.190 --> 07:47.830
"Hot Spring"

07:47.830 --> 07:51.100
"Hot Spring"
Aguascolientes...

07:51.100 --> 07:52.770
"Hot Spring"

07:52.770 --> 07:54.170
"Hot Spring"
So there's a hot spring here...

07:54.170 --> 07:55.140
So there's a hot spring here...

07:55.140 --> 07:57.940
What the heck? How weird.

07:57.940 --> 07:59.540
It's weird?

07:59.540 --> 08:01.080
Do you know what Japón is?

08:01.080 --> 08:02.810
The name of a foreign country.

08:02.810 --> 08:04.080
That's all you know?

08:04.080 --> 08:06.050
A small country in the east,

08:06.050 --> 08:12.150
where people called geisha
paint tempura and eat "samurice"...

08:12.150 --> 08:16.660
- You're pretty knowledgeable.
- Common knowledge.

08:16.660 --> 08:21.230
But I hear that "ogals" and " kotakus"
are all the rage there now.

08:21.230 --> 08:22.260
That's news to me.

08:22.260 --> 08:25.230
- Right?
- So?

08:25.230 --> 08:26.030
"Hot Spring"
- Right?
- So?

08:26.030 --> 08:30.100
"Hot Spring"
It says that this is a
Japón-style hot spring, but...

08:30.100 --> 08:32.110
"Hot Spring"
It's pretty sketchy, isn't it?

08:32.110 --> 08:34.210
"Hot Spring"
Yeah, sketchy.

08:34.210 --> 08:34.540
Yeah, sketchy.

08:37.780 --> 08:39.650
Where are they going?

08:39.650 --> 08:39.710
"Hot Spring"
Where are they going?

08:39.710 --> 08:44.620
"Hot Spring"

08:47.820 --> 08:49.760
We wasted our time coming here.

08:51.060 --> 08:52.720
Ellis?

09:05.240 --> 09:09.710
Many life forms were created
with the DNA of witches.

09:09.710 --> 09:14.320
But they all turned out to be failures.

09:14.320 --> 09:16.280
With the exception of you...

09:16.280 --> 09:18.910
...and me.

09:20.860 --> 09:22.250
What's wrong?!

09:26.830 --> 09:28.330
How do you feel?

09:28.330 --> 09:30.000
I'm fine now.

09:30.000 --> 09:32.700
Okay, then that's good.

09:32.700 --> 09:34.900
I'm worried, too.

09:34.900 --> 09:37.240
Worried about you.

09:37.240 --> 09:38.870
Why?

09:38.870 --> 09:41.640
Because you're being weird.

09:47.680 --> 09:50.910
Good-bye, Nadie.

09:55.860 --> 09:57.990
Ellis...

09:57.990 --> 09:59.330
The truth is...

09:59.330 --> 10:01.320
There's something I need to tell you...

10:03.830 --> 10:05.370
It's dark.

10:05.370 --> 10:07.870
Long time no see.

10:07.870 --> 10:10.740
- Lirio.
- You two again?

10:10.740 --> 10:14.080
You keep following us around.
What exactly is it that you're after?

10:14.080 --> 10:17.110
- Don't make baseless accusations.
- Don't play dumb.

10:17.110 --> 10:19.610
You're the ones who came after us.

10:19.610 --> 10:22.050
Huh? But...

10:29.920 --> 10:34.360
Pisses me off! Why do I have
to do something like this?!

10:34.360 --> 10:36.160
There! There!

10:36.160 --> 10:38.860
- Don't put it back in!
- I got yelled at.

10:49.980 --> 10:52.910
- I'm tired.
- It was tiring.

10:52.910 --> 10:55.210
You didn't do anything!

10:58.350 --> 11:02.190
- What?
- You want us to bathe in
the hot spring together?

11:09.760 --> 11:11.430
That feels good!

11:14.270 --> 11:16.840
You're not going in?

11:16.840 --> 11:18.930
- No.
- I see.

11:29.320 --> 11:32.010
- Nadie!
- Coming!

11:36.990 --> 11:41.930
Ah, this is nice!

12:26.040 --> 12:29.170
I trust none of you have any objections?

12:35.350 --> 12:37.520
I've received instructions from our superiors.

12:37.520 --> 12:40.150
They've decided to take Ellis into safe custody.

12:40.150 --> 12:42.290
We know where to find them, I assume?

12:42.290 --> 12:43.980
Of course.

12:50.230 --> 12:51.930
Push.

13:02.380 --> 13:05.510
Looking rather glum there.

13:05.510 --> 13:06.980
Oh, it's you.

13:06.980 --> 13:10.040
Name's Ricardo. Want a drink?

13:11.550 --> 13:13.210
Thanks.

13:19.330 --> 13:23.260
It looks like this may be
the last time we run into you.

13:23.260 --> 13:24.530
What do you mean?

13:24.530 --> 13:26.400
My contract's run out.

13:26.400 --> 13:28.140
Contract?

13:28.140 --> 13:32.240
So, you were working for someone...

13:32.240 --> 13:34.000
Who?

13:35.580 --> 13:37.410
I forget.

13:43.020 --> 13:45.320
We'll leave after sundown.

13:45.320 --> 13:49.050
Play with Lirio for me until then.

13:53.190 --> 13:56.260
You're right. This is fun.

13:56.260 --> 13:59.570
That girl...

13:59.570 --> 14:02.900
- She's not family, is she?
- Couldn't really say.

14:02.900 --> 14:05.530
She's too cute to be your daughter anyway.

14:07.580 --> 14:09.980
Are things going well for you?

14:09.980 --> 14:14.110
Lirio trusts me.

14:14.110 --> 14:15.880
That's all.

14:59.060 --> 15:00.920
It's me.

15:02.160 --> 15:05.500
I'm going out for a bit.
Look after Ellis for me.

15:05.500 --> 15:07.570
Are you sure about this?

15:07.570 --> 15:11.400
It's not you that I trust. It's Lirio.

15:38.130 --> 15:39.700
It's been a long time.

15:39.700 --> 15:43.270
When was it that we last met?

15:43.270 --> 15:44.570
I don't remember.

15:44.570 --> 15:46.310
Have you lost a little weight?

15:46.310 --> 15:48.980
As for you, you seem to have...

15:48.980 --> 15:51.350
- Never mind.
- Why?

15:51.350 --> 15:54.710
Because I don't want to offend my client.

15:57.050 --> 15:59.140
That was unpleasant enough as it was.

16:00.290 --> 16:01.980
What's this?

16:04.190 --> 16:05.590
Your payment.

16:05.590 --> 16:11.230
15% has been added on top of what
you demanded when we hired you.

16:11.230 --> 16:12.670
What's going on here?

16:12.670 --> 16:15.100
Your contract ends today.

16:20.240 --> 16:23.510
I sense you, Ellis.

16:23.510 --> 16:26.480
I can tell.

16:26.480 --> 16:30.180
I can smell your scent...

16:30.180 --> 16:33.390
Hold on a minute! This is too sudden!

16:33.390 --> 16:35.320
I'm grateful to you.

16:35.320 --> 16:38.160
For protecting Ellis until today.

16:38.160 --> 16:40.060
What's going to happen to her?

16:40.060 --> 16:42.730
I have no need to tell you that.

16:42.730 --> 16:46.170
Stay out of her business from now on.

16:52.610 --> 16:54.170
You can have it back.

16:54.170 --> 16:57.310
- So, there you have it.
- Wait.

16:57.310 --> 17:00.450
I've made up my mind.

17:00.450 --> 17:03.550
That I'm going to stay by Ellis's side.

17:03.550 --> 17:06.650
Don't say such childish things.

17:06.650 --> 17:10.690
I'm talking business here.

17:10.690 --> 17:12.560
Grow up.

17:28.680 --> 17:31.150
I've come for you,

17:31.150 --> 17:33.410
Ellis.

17:33.410 --> 17:35.210
Stay away.

17:44.190 --> 17:45.680
Wait!

17:54.130 --> 17:55.830
Hide-and-seek?!

17:58.070 --> 18:00.370
Where are you? Where are you, Ellis?!

18:00.370 --> 18:02.100
Lirio!

18:17.320 --> 18:18.860
Are you both all right?

18:18.860 --> 18:20.430
Watch out!

18:20.430 --> 18:22.120
Up there!

18:24.570 --> 18:27.870
You have my thanks.

18:27.870 --> 18:31.770
I came very close to harming Ellis.

18:31.770 --> 18:33.670
Just who are you?!

18:33.670 --> 18:37.610
Thank you for protecting my Ellis.

18:37.610 --> 18:39.780
Pardon?

18:39.780 --> 18:43.120
I'm L.A.

18:43.120 --> 18:48.460
The man who was born to be bound with Ellis.

18:48.460 --> 18:50.790
You may not know this,

18:50.790 --> 18:55.500
but we've met many times.

18:55.500 --> 18:58.900
- ls that true?
- We met the other day, too.

18:58.900 --> 19:01.870
He said...

19:01.870 --> 19:04.130
...that I'm not human.

19:15.880 --> 19:18.350
I'll come again.

19:18.350 --> 19:23.290
Until then, look after my Ellis for me...

19:32.230 --> 19:35.830
I... hate him.

19:53.250 --> 19:56.460
So, you knew.

19:56.460 --> 19:59.730
Yes, I knew.

19:59.730 --> 20:02.300
Why didn't you tell me?

20:02.300 --> 20:05.530
Because you didn't ask.

20:05.530 --> 20:08.400
- Right.
- You knew, too.

20:08.400 --> 20:09.670
Huh?

20:09.670 --> 20:12.810
W-Well, yeah.

20:12.810 --> 20:14.370
Doesn't it bother you?

20:14.370 --> 20:16.740
What?

20:16.740 --> 20:20.370
That I'm not human.

20:24.890 --> 20:28.620
Don't say such sad things.

20:28.620 --> 20:30.390
Nadie...

20:35.700 --> 20:37.490
Yessir.

20:56.450 --> 20:59.020
It's your turn, Doug.

20:59.020 --> 21:02.920
Queen to bishop 6. Check.

21:06.790 --> 21:09.560
I'll take your queen with my knight.

21:09.560 --> 21:14.020
Bishop to king 2. Checkmate.

21:17.370 --> 21:21.010
The Council will now be brought to a close.

21:21.010 --> 21:24.030
We give our thanks to the
spirits of our distant ancestors.

21:27.350 --> 21:29.750
You win, Doug.

21:30.950 --> 21:33.650
Yes, that's right...

21:37.860 --> 21:40.020
I win.

21:53.970 --> 21:56.940
Is something the matter?

21:56.940 --> 21:58.610
That girl Nadie...

21:58.610 --> 22:02.380
- What?
- It's nothing.

22:02.380 --> 22:05.920
Where is your swimsuit?

22:05.920 --> 22:09.360
In Japanese spas, this is the proper attire.

22:22.100 --> 22:24.840
Nadie voided her contract,

22:24.840 --> 22:27.570
and her resolve to continue traveling with Ellis

22:27.570 --> 22:31.010
as an individual human being...

22:31.010 --> 22:32.910
...was hardened.

22:36.550 --> 22:40.350
Like a neverending summer

22:40.350 --> 22:43.790
Like flowers that never die

22:43.790 --> 22:47.690
Those arms you've wrapped around me

22:47.690 --> 22:55.830
Don't ever let go of me

23:02.040 --> 23:05.650
Even if I try clinging to you

23:05.650 --> 23:11.450
My heart still heeds a different evanescence

23:11.450 --> 23:15.420
Counting the rhythm of time by it

23:15.420 --> 23:19.530
A night of red stars

23:19.530 --> 23:23.530
The vanishing warmth

23:23.530 --> 23:27.470
I want to keep it here

23:27.470 --> 23:33.870
You, with your eyes closed

23:33.870 --> 23:37.840
Yearning over and over

23:37.840 --> 23:41.180
Even if I can't go anywhere

23:41.180 --> 23:45.420
When the heartache comes to a stop

23:45.420 --> 23:51.730
To the two of us, this moment is...

23:51.730 --> 23:56.720
...everything
